# Words that must never appear in this repository, as SHA-256 digests of the
# lowercase word, one per line. scripts/check-denylist.mjs splits every tracked
# text file, the fixtures and the built bundles into lowercase [a-z0-9]+ words
# and fails on any word whose digest is listed here; `pnpm test` and CI run it.
#
# To add a word, hash it in lowercase with no trailing newline, and put the
# digest on a line of its own:
#
#   printf %s word | shasum -a 256
#
# Never write the word itself here, in a commit message or in a pull request:
# the digests exist so that the list does not publish what it lists. Words are
# matched whole, so a name written in several words needs a digest for each
# word that must not appear, and one for the run-together form.
#
# The self-test word of packages/cli/test/denylist.test.ts, which plants it to
# prove the check fails:
5409dfdc8f2c9b71c34c0085e168cd5978642573a36251e39bc3c1ab2123af77

# Private project terms (digests only; the words are never committed).
